## Standalone Minimum Gate

This repository must remain usable without personal global Agent rules or optional global Skills:

1. Before editing, summarize the goal, in/out of scope, acceptance criteria, affected modules/files, and ambiguities/risks. Ask before editing when ambiguity changes behavior, contracts, data, permissions, billing, security, or workflow.
2. Treat assumptions as temporary working hypotheses. Before implementation, test expectations, canonical documentation, or delivery, resolve every material assumption as verified evidence or an explicit user decision; otherwise remove the assumption and clean up dependent plans, tests, docs, and edits. Any remaining hypothesis must be non-material, harmless, reversible, unable to affect behavior or risk, and state its checkpoint. Preserve a non-blocking unknown only as an open question or evidence gap without a presumed answer.
3. Inspect the existing Owner, similar implementations, reusable modules, dependency boundaries, test locations, generators, and verification commands. Do not add parallel logic without justification.
4. For bugs, preserve a focused pre-fix failure and repeat it after the fix; keep a permanent regression test only when it protects observable behavior, a stable contract/invariant, a known regression, or a meaningful boundary with an independent expected result. For features, test only affected happy, invalid, edge, permission/state, and nearby regression cases. Start with focused verification, broaden once when cross-owner risk requires it, and do not run both an aggregate gate and its contained targets on unchanged inputs merely to repeat the same suites.
5. Before delivery, report requirement match, design/reuse decisions, changed and generated files, commands and results, remaining risks, and rollback/recovery notes when relevant.

Optional global rules may provide stricter or more detailed guidance when installed; this section is the repository-local fallback, not a second full engineering standard.
